  isbn      = {9783031292491},
  pages     = {79--95},
  abstract  = {The modern researches in field of cryolite melts containing silica were considered in this chapter. They are as follows: 1) Development of novel fluoroaluminate electrolytes with lower working temperatures based on potassium cryolite melts. 2) Further investigations of physico-chemical and electrochemical properties of cryolite–silica melts. The main purposes of these studies are the electrolytes for production of solar grade silicon rather than Al–Si alloys. 3) Processing of the spent pot lining. 4) Production of oxygen and metal alloys by electrolysis of lunar soils by means of the electrolysis of cryolite melts. 5) Use of sodium hexafluorosilicate to obtain Al–Si alloy and cryolite in aluminum electrolyzers. The works of recent years discussed in this chapter confirm our earlier conclusions about the stability and chemical reactions in Na3AlF6–Al2O3–SiO2 melts, as well as about the causes of technological violations and ways to eliminate them. Essentially, no new and significant results have been obtained.},
